      "writtenOn": "2024-11-16T02:48:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e static counter can be used for more than identify a socket.\n\nPlease explain, I am not familiar with the CL you have attached, nor was I part of the review then",
      "parentUuid": "38730d89_bf77a88d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1114,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1120,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "32cf46dea2638eb27e709ba596e0f11eee0904b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e43dffcb_7ca15431",
        "filename": "system/btif/src/btif_sock_l2cap.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1120,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T03:13:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One case I can think of is when offload application A requests to release a channel for an identifier that it is not allocated to, and since static counters make it very easy to \bestimate adjacent identifiers, there is a need to take separate protection methods at multiple layers for this case.\n\nAnd based on the identifier based on the static counter, it is possible to predict how many sockets are currently in use in the system, and it seems that there is a possibility of abuse along with the first reason.",
      "parentUuid": "f29e4cc6_951ed81e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1114,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1120,
        "endChar": 1
      },
